1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,480
Here's the problem, AI agents are about to move money on chain, and one agent is just

2
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:07,160
one confident boy holding the keys.

3
00:00:08,060 --> 00:00:08,919
I'm not okay with that.

4
00:00:09,820 --> 00:00:11,179
Quorum proof is a fleet.

5
00:00:11,679 --> 00:00:13,560
No single agent can move value alone.

6
00:00:14,259 --> 00:00:18,219
Every decision needs a quorum, and the fact they argue over is verified by Creditcoin

7
00:00:18,219 --> 00:00:18,519
itself.

8
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:21,579
Not an oracle operator in the middle, the chain itself.

9
00:00:23,179 --> 00:00:27,820
Look at this. It's a real run, not a mock. That's a real Ethereum mainnet transaction,

10
00:00:28,339 --> 00:00:33,979
3.6 ETH. A test coin proves it inside CreditCoin's own trust domain. Build the proof,

11
00:00:34,439 --> 00:00:40,060
verify it with the block prover precompile on CC3 testnet, decoded on-chain into a structured fact.

12
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:45,920
And it's all reads, zero tokens, zero keys. I don't need to spend anything to prove a fact.

13
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:52,579
Now the fleet, three agents, three mandates, not three copies of the same model.

14
00:00:53,060 --> 00:00:54,899
The underwriter wants exact policy fit.

15
00:00:55,340 --> 00:00:56,899
The fraud hunter asks one question.

16
00:00:57,299 --> 00:00:58,219
Is this transaction real?

17
00:00:58,740 --> 00:01:00,679
The market analyst reads partial repayments.

18
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:03,500
Round one is a secret ballot.

19
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:05,700
Everyone commits before anyone sees a vote.

20
00:01:06,439 --> 00:01:09,040
Round two is debate, and each agent can revise once.

21
00:01:10,260 --> 00:01:12,980
Watch the repayment case, three out of three.

22
00:01:13,599 --> 00:01:16,760
Execute the certificate sealed. Every ballot signature verified.

23
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:20,260
Now an unrelated inflow, watch the split.

24
00:01:20,780 --> 00:01:24,819
The fraud hunter says yes, the transaction's real, its integrity check passes.

25
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:26,760
The other two say no on policy.

26
00:01:27,219 --> 00:01:28,060
This isn't a repayment.

27
00:01:28,879 --> 00:01:30,480
One out of three, reject.

28
00:01:31,599 --> 00:01:34,920
The quorum blocks it, and the sole dissent is right there on the record.

29
00:01:35,379 --> 00:01:36,400
That's the product working.

30
00:01:38,019 --> 00:01:44,019
Every ballot signed with the agent's own CEP256K1 key and bound to the ATAS coin fact hash.

31
00:01:44,599 --> 00:01:49,799
On chain, the Quorum Registry contract recovers every signature and applies the Quorum gate,

32
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:56,420
two of three. Deploy it and the decision becomes a credit coin fact. One, any lending protocol can consume.

33
00:01:58,060 --> 00:02:02,219
Quorum-proof, auditable, autonomous decisions on the ATESCOIN protocol.

34
00:02:03,159 --> 00:02:06,299
The fleet replaces the Oracle and the paper trail is the product.
